  "description": "Infest is the second studio album and major label debut by American rock band Papa Roach. It was released on April 25, 2000, through DreamWorks Records. The sound on the album is mainly classified as nu metal and rap metal, with many songs containing rapped vocals and hip hop influences. It was certified 4× Platinum in the U.S. by the RIAA on December 6, 2024, making it the band's best-selling album, peaked at No. 5 on the Billboard 200 chart, and became the 20th highest-selling album of 2000 in the United States. Infest earned Papa Roach a Grammy Award nomination for Best New Artist.",
